    "body": "Part of epic #2; depends on backend foundation (#4).\n\n## Goal\nTrack parts and accessories relevant to JD repair work so the owner can see actual on-hand stock, what is reserved/used, and what must be sourced.\n\n## Scope\n- Part catalogue: SKU/internal code, name, category, compatible brands/models (where known), unit, cost price, selling price, supplier, location/bin, minimum stock and active status.\n- Stock receipts, adjustments, reservations, consumption against a service job, returns and damaged/obsolete stock as immutable movement records.\n- Current quantity derived from the movement ledger; no silent overwrites.\n- Low-stock/reorder list and supplier contact/reference records.\n- Support parts sourced per job when not held in stock; clearly distinguish in-stock, reserved, ordered and unavailable.\n- Optional serial/batch tracking only where useful for a part category.\n- Role/permission and audit rules; owner approval for stock adjustments.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Stock cannot become negative without an explicitly authorized override with reason.\n- Every movement records part, quantity, direction, reason, related job/reference, actor and timestamp.\n- Tests cover receipt, use, return, adjustment, concurrent updates and reorder threshold.\n- CRM/job detail shows parts used and cost impact.\n- No invented stock quantity or supplier availability.",
